This project is an independent Rust implementation of an Oblivious HTTP
(RFC 9458) gateway. It does not contain source code copied from Cloudflare's
`privacy-gateway-server-go`, but its behavior was deliberately modeled on
that project as a functional reference, and its X25519 key-derivation
transform is intentionally byte-for-byte compatible with it (see
`docs/adr/0001-preserve-x25519-seed-derivation.md`). Portions of this
project's behavior are therefore adapted from:

  privacy-gateway-server-go
  Copyright (c) 2022, Cloudflare, Inc.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  https://github.com/cloudflare/privacy-gateway-server-go

See LICENSE for this project's license terms (BSD 3-Clause, matching the
reference implementation above).

Third-party Rust crate dependency licenses were reviewed via `cargo
metadata` against the locked dependency graph (`Cargo.lock`). Every
dependency declares a permissive license (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause,
ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0, BSL-1.0, or Unlicense, in
various dual/multi-license combinations); none are copyleft. This is an
enforced CI gate, not just a one-time manual check: `deny.toml` encodes
the same allow-list, and the `deny` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs
`cargo deny check licenses`, `check bans sources`, and (soft-gated,
`continue-on-error`) `check advisories` on every push and pull request.
Run it locally with:

    cargo deny check licenses
    cargo deny check bans sources
    cargo deny check advisories

